            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bgrayii"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really enjoyed it, using home grown cilantro (very strong) and extra parmesan. Others that I shared it with liked it but were not as excited about it as myself, as they were not big cilantro fans. If you like cilantro you gotta try this!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CookinBug"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Let me start by saying, I love garlic every which way... except raw. By the time the eggs were cooked properly, the garlic was still pretty raw. I really wish I would have sauteed the garlic separately before adding the eggs. I loved the cilantro and thought it was the perfect amount, but the garlic killed it for me. I'll make these again, but cook the garlic a bit first. Thanks :)",
            "datePublished": "2009-04-25T07:43:29.830Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gina McNay"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious- I had some ingredients in fridge I wanted to use up, so I added a couple things. I sautéed the garlic with cumin and diced jalapeño and red onion, then added the eggs (with the cilantro and extra sour cream bc I am out of milk) added salt and pepper to taste. I added extra fresh cilantro on top (I LOVE cilantro &amp; it’s good for you!!), some chili lime hot sauce, &amp; some salsa verde. YUM! Thanks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-06T15:32:29.923Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cleo1076"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The cilantro gave the dish a very fresh taste but was a bit overwhelming. I'll cut down to 1 TBS next time. And, even though I love garlic, I'll be sure to use a smaller clove next time. But we did enjoy it - yum, sour cream - and will make again, perhaps as an omelet with cheese inside! Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2007-03-24T07:16:36.550Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LOJ371"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a nice variation to the boring scrambled egg. I made it exactly as written - here is what I will change next time I make it: instead of garlic, I will use garlic powder, I will add chopped onion and omit the parm cheese. A little hot sauce, and I think it will be perfect! I eat an egg everyday and was looking for a new way to prepare - this is the perfect canvass to build on in my opinion. (I didn't use the full amount of cilantro)",
            "datePublished": "2008-10-22T07:19:57.300Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "angie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was absolutely delicious and my family loved it. Instead of parmesean cheese I used feta cheese and it was soooo good. I had to substitute the cilantro with parsley. I will try cilantro next time but it was delicous anyway. I will be making this again and again.",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-30T15:42:18.383Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
